<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54523" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταμηλόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>put in the probe</i>, so as to sound wounds, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, etc.; or to produce vomiting, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμει καταμηλῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phryn.Com.
					62
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κημὸν κ</span>.
			<i>use</i> the funnel of the ballot-jar <i>as a probe</i>, i.e.
				<i>make</i> a peculator <i>disgorge</i> what he has stolen,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1150
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τὰ ἔρια</span>
			<i>plunge</i> them into dyestuff, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.169
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
